		    EVA Player for Sunrise ATA-IDE ver 0.07
		    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Description:
~~~~~~~~~~~~

EVA is the video format design by ESE Artist's Factory. With MSX TurboR +
MegaSCSI interface through a Sony HB-V1 digitizer you can record animated
sequences in screen 12, 128*106 pixels, 10 or 12 fps and digital sound with
15,75 KHz. For see and play the EVAS was necessary a MSX TurboR and a MegaSCSI
interface.

System Requeriments:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

EvaIDE doesn't use MegaSCSI interface. This version only works with Sunrise
ATA-IDE interface. It works fine with MSX TurboR, but also works perfectly
with MSX2+. To get sound with MSX2+, it plays through Philips Music Module
cartridge or a Covox card.

This program has been designed to work with Z80 (3,57 MHz). MSX2+ Panasonic
A1-WX (WSX) and TurboR have Z80A and R800 processors (6 and 28 MHz); in this
case (if they are enable) it doesn't matter: the program will change the
processor automatically. The owners of a MSX with Z80H (7 MHz) must change
the mode of the processor manually.

Is recommended to use a fast LBA Hard Disk. In spite of that, the player
supports perfectly CHS mode of HDs (but the video will lose smoothness, and
sound will lose quality).

EvaIDE should work with any Bios from ATA-IDE interface.


Execution and options:
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

From command line:

EVAIDE [letter:][\path\]evafile.eva [/V] [/W] [/A] [/C] [/8] [/M] [/Snn] [/Enn]

where [/x] are optional.
It's necessary that the letter (where EVA is) must be defragmented.

Options:

	/V -> Disable the syncronization with the screen refresh.
	      Use this option if you realize that the play is slow.

	/W -> Disable the sync. of the sound.
	      This option only works with PCM of MSX TurboR and allow to win
	      speed althoughyou lose sound quality.

	/A -> Force the use of Music Module. This option only works with MSX
	      TurboR.

	/X -> Force the use of Covox. By default sound plays through Music
	      Module on MSX2+ machines.

	/C -> Force 12fps mode.

	/8 -> Force screen 8.

	/M -> Force R800 ROM mode in MSX TurboR or 6 MHz in Panasonic
	      A1-WX/WSX instead Z80 standard (3,57 MHz)

	/L -> Loop mode. Playback restarts at end.

	/Snn -> Specify the first frame of the EVA.

	/Enn -> Specify the final frame of the EVA.


